<Project>

  <!--
    Lodestar.Decomposition owns its version here, independently of the other
    packages (see docs/decisions/0012-per-package-versioning.md).

    0.1.0 was this package's first release. It carries one inter-package edge, to
    Lodestar.Abstractions, whose floor lives in src/Directory.Packages.props and
    is deliberately decoupled from this number.

    0.1.1 is a patch because Nmf.Fit's widened component bound (#519) takes
    nothing away: no signature moved and no member was removed, so every call
    that compiled against 0.1.0 still compiles and still returns what it did.
    What changed is a precondition relaxed — componentCount at
    min(RowCount, ColumnCount) threw ArgumentOutOfRangeException and now fits,
    which is scikit-learn's own bound and therefore a parity defect repaired
    rather than a feature added. This number must stay ahead of the feed: 0.1.0
    shipped on 2026-09-01, and nuget.org is immutable, so a declared version
    that collides with a published one makes two different assemblies answer to
    the same identity.

    0.3.0 is a minor release because PrincipalComponentVariance (#701) is a new
    public type and nothing was removed or changed: every call that compiled
    against 0.2.0 still compiles and still returns what it did. 0.2.0 is
    published, so the addition takes the next minor number rather than joining it.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <LodestarDecompositionVersion>0.3.0</LodestarDecompositionVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
